  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Gunfire and military vehicles are reported near the Presidential Palace in N'Djamena, Chad, with the Chadian government accusing Boko Haram of being behind the attack. The Chad National Army has reportedly regained stable control of the capital, with 18 insurgents and one security force member being killed in the attack. ((Devdiscourse)) ((Deutsche Welle))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israeli airstrikes across the Gaza Strip kill at least 22 people. ((Arab News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Russian forces attack an industrial facility in Zaporizhzhia, Ukraine, killing 13 people and injuring 18 others. Further strikes on Zaporizhzhia with guided aerial bombs kill 13 more people and injure 32 others. ((Ukrainska Pravda)) ((Ukrainska Pravda 2))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "More than 100,000 people are evacuated from approaching wildfires in the Pacific Palisades and Hollywood neighborhoods of Los Angeles and Altadena, California, United States, that have burnt more than 3,000 acres, aggravated by an ongoing extreme windstorm and drought conditions. Five people are killed, dozens of others are injured, and around 1,000 structures are destroyed. ((AP)) ((The Independent)) ((NBC News)) ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Six people are killed and over forty others are injured in a stampede at the Hindu Venkateswara Temple in Tirupati, Andhra Pradesh, India. ((AP)) ((Business Today))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "The Iranian government releases Italian journalist Cecilia Sala from prison, with Sala arriving back in Rome later that day. ((Euronews)) ((Yahoo! News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "Lithuanian prime minister Gintautas Paluckas deploys the police to secure the country's electricity link with Poland in response to reported attempts to disrupt the planned decoupling of the Baltic states' power systems from the grid shared with Belarus and Russia. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "Azerbaijan protests Eritrea's detention of three Azerbaijani-flagged vessels and 18 crew members since November 2024, stating the ships entered Eritrean waters due to adverse weather en route to Abu Dhabi, United Arab Emirates. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "The British government freezes the assets of neo-Nazi music network Blood & Honour, becoming the first far-right group in the UK to be sanctioned by the government. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israeli airstrikes across the Gaza Strip kill at least 27 people. ((Arab News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Twenty-eight soldiers are killed during a mass shooting in northern Benin near the border with Burkina Faso. ((Punch))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "The ruling party in São Tomé and Príncipe, Independent Democratic Action, proposes Hélio Vaz de Almeida as Prime Minister to replace Patrice Trovoada, who was fired by President Carlos Vila Nova two days ago. ((RFI))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "The CALNEV Pipeline connecting oil refineries in southern California to Clark County, Nevada, shuts down due to power outages, temporarily cutting off the gasoline supply to Las Vegas and Nellis Air Force Base. The Kinder Morgan SFPP Pipeline connecting southern California to Phoenix, Arizona, also shuts down. ((KTNV)) ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Politics and elections",
      "text": "Alcide Ponga of the pro-France The Rally party is elected President of New Caledonia by six of the eleven government ministers. ((Radio New Zealand))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "At least 40 people are killed and 12 others are injured in Tatmadaw airstrikes on Ramree, Rakhine State, Myanmar. ((Al Jazeera)) ((India Today))"
    }
  ],
